{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "NoahSoilHeat",
  "description": "Soil heat diffusion and the surface energy balance that closes it, in WRF's unified Noah land-surface model: SUBROUTINE TDFCND (soil thermal conductivity), the heat-capacity and flux-divergence parts of SUBROUTINE HRT, the yy/zz1 closure NOPAC forms before calling SHFLX, and the skin temperature and ground heat flux SHFLX returns (phys/module_sf_noahlsm.F, WRF 4.8, sf_surface_physics = 2), written as instantaneous tendencies. THE PDE: hcpct dT/dt = d/dz( df dT/dz ) on a column of NLEV soil layers, written as the flux-form operator D(K_soil D(T_soil) - F_soil) and lowered by the EarthSciDiscretizations column_nonuniform_1d rule varcoeff_face_flux_laplacian_lev, exactly as the slab scheme does. Orientation: `lev` is the soil layer index with layer 1 at the surface and `ze` the interface DEPTH below ground (positive downward, ze[1] = 0, increasing with the index), so ze is the negative of WRF's ZSOIL prefixed by zero. TWO boundary fluxes close the column and both are prescribed, which is why the diffusive part at the two domain faces is dropped: the surface interface carries F_soil[1] = df1 (yy - stc[1])/(0.5 ze[2] zz1), which is (the negative of) the Fortran's SSOIL and is the linearised surface energy balance rather than a temperature gradient; and the bottom interface carries the conduction to the prescribed deep-soil temperature, F_soil[NLEV+1] = df[NLEV] (stc[NLEV] - tbot)/(z_deep - zc[NLEV]). THE CONDUCTIVITY IS NOT FACE-AVERAGED. WRF evaluates TDFCND at the layer centre and then uses that one value for the flux through the layer's LOWER face, so the coefficient at interface kn is the conductivity of the layer ABOVE it, K_soil[kn] = df[kn-1]; a centred average would be the textbook choice and is NOT what the Fortran does, so the component reproduces the Fortran (FORTRAN_BUGS N90). The top layer's conductivity additionally carries the canopy reduction df1 = df[1] exp(sbeta shdfac), which the Fortran applies in NOPAC but not inside HRT's loop, so it appears at interface 2 and in the surface flux and nowhere else. THE SURFACE CLOSURE: yy and zz1 are NOPAC's linearisation of the skin-temperature energy balance about the air temperature; the skin temperature is DIAGNOSTIC, t1 = (yy + (zz1 - 1) stc[1])/zz1, not a prognostic state, and the reported ground heat flux ssoil = df1 (stc[1] - t1)/(0.5 ze[2]) is WRF's sign convention (positive warms the surface) and therefore the NEGATIVE of F_soil[1]. The sensible heat flux is evaluated at that diagnostic skin temperature and uses cp = 1004.5 and rd = 287.04, unlike SUBROUTINE PENMAN's rch (FORTRAN_BUGS N88). NOT TRANSCRIBED, and a consumer must not mount this component where they matter: the soil-water phase change (SNKSRC/TMPAVG/TBND, which adds a latent sink to the tendency of any layer holding ice or lying below 273.15 K), the snow-pack branch (SNOPAC), the urban override (df = 3.24, csoil = 3e6) and the opt_thcnd = 2 McCumber conductivity for silt/clay loam. The reference set is entirely above freezing and snow-free, so the freezing branch is UNTESTED here, not merely unused. Consumer-supplied column fields (ze, stc, smc, sh2o) are rewrite-target ops `input_<name>` lowered by the consumer, in the inline tests through per-test expression_template_imports libraries generated by tools/fill_tests.py.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "land-surface",
   "noah",
   "soil-heat-diffusion",
   "surface-energy-balance",
   "column",
   "pde"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Peters-Lidard, C. D., et al. (1998). The effect of soil thermal conductivity parameterization on surface energy fluxes and temperatures. J. Atmos. Sci., 55, 1209-1224."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Johansen, O. (1975). Thermal conductivity of soils. Ph.D. thesis, University of Trondheim."
   },
   {
    "citation": "Chen, F., and J. Dudhia (2001). Coupling an advanced land surface-hydrology model with the Penn State-NCAR MM5 modeling system. Part I. Mon. Wea. Rev., 129, 569-585."
   },
   {
    "citation": "wrf-model/WRF v4.8.0 phys/module_sf_noahlsm.F SUBROUTINE TDFCND lines 4124-4247, HRT lines 1588-1850, SHFLX lines 2600-2666 and the NOPAC closure lines 2168-2180 (instrumented in ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170, commit ac6d4cc; the internal df1/yy/zz1 are published by kernels/noah_esm_*.inc)."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 4,
   "description": "Number of soil layers, WRF num_soil_layers (4 for the Noah default). Bound into the column grid at the import edge."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "NoahSoilHeat": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/varcoeff_face_flux_laplacian_lev.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    }
   ],
   "subsystems": {
    "wrf": {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
    },
    "par": {
     "ref": "./noah_parameters.esm"
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "ze": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Soil layer interface DEPTHS below the surface, positive downward, ze[1] = 0; the negative of WRF's ZSOIL prefixed by zero."
    },
    "zc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Soil layer centre depths, from the grid's column_cell_center template. Reproduces the midpoints WRF forms implicitly in HRT's 0.5 (zsoil(k-1) - zsoil(k+1)) denominators."
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Soil layer thicknesses, from the grid's column_cell_thickness template. Equals WRF's SLDPTH."
    },
    "stc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Soil temperature of each layer, WRF's STC. Read as a plain algebraic input: the consumer owns the state and integrates dstc_dt."
    },
    "smc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "TOTAL volumetric soil moisture of each layer, WRF's SMC."
    },
    "sh2o": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "UNFROZEN volumetric soil water of each layer, WRF's SH2O. Equals smc wherever the soil is above freezing."
    },
    "quartz": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.25,
     "description": "Quartz volume fraction of the soil type, SOILPARM.TBL QTZ, which sets the solid-phase conductivity."
    },
    "smcmax": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m^3/m^3",
     "default": 0.476,
     "description": "Soil porosity (saturation moisture) of the soil type, SOILPARM.TBL MAXSMC."
    },
    "shdfac": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.5,
     "description": "Green vegetation fraction, WRF's SHDFAC, which reduces the surface-layer conductivity through exp(sbeta shdfac)."
    },
    "sfctmp": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 300.0,
     "description": "Air temperature at the lowest model level, WRF's SFCTMP."
    },
    "sfcprs": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "Pa",
     "default": 100000.0,
     "description": "Air pressure at the lowest model level, WRF's SFCPRS."
    },
    "th2": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 300.0,
     "description": "Potential temperature at the lowest model level referenced to the surface pressure, WRF's TH2."
    },
    "q2": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "kg/kg",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "Specific humidity at the lowest model level, WRF's Q2, used for the virtual temperature in the sensible-heat flux."
    },
    "ch": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m/s",
     "default": 0.01,
     "description": "Surface exchange coefficient for heat and moisture, WRF's CH."
    },
    "fdown": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "default": 600.0,
     "description": "Total absorbed downward radiation at the surface, WRF's FDOWN = solnet + lwdn."
    },
    "emissi": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.985,
     "description": "Surface emissivity, WRF's EMISSI."
    },
    "rch": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "W/(m^2*K)",
     "default": 10.0,
     "description": "Bulk heat-transfer coefficient in energy units from the Penman component, WRF's RCH. Carries PENMAN's cp = 1004.6."
    },
    "rr": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 2.0,
     "description": "Resistance ratio from the Penman component, WRF's RR."
    },
    "epsca": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 10.0,
     "description": "Penman potential evaporation expressed as a temperature, WRF's EPSCA."
    },
    "beta": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "1",
     "default": 0.6,
     "description": "Ratio of actual to potential evaporation from the evapotranspiration component, WRF's BETA. The product beta epsca is the latent-heat term of the surface energy balance."
    },
    "tbot": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "K",
     "default": 300.0,
     "description": "Prescribed deep-soil temperature at depth z_deep, WRF's TBOT."
    },
    "z_deep": {
     "type": "parameter",
     "units": "m",
     "default": 8.0,
     "description": "Depth at which tbot is prescribed, |ZBOT_DATA| = 8 m. Positive downward, matching ze."
    },
    "df_raw": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/(m*K)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Johansen/Peters-Lidard soil thermal conductivity of each layer from TDFCND (opt_thcnd = 1): the dry value thkdry raised towards the saturated value thksat by the Kersten number ake."
    },
    "df_layer": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/(m*K)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "df_raw with the canopy reduction applied to the SURFACE LAYER ONLY, df[1] exp(sbeta shdfac). WRF applies it in NOPAC, after HRT's interior loop has already used the unreduced values, so only the top layer and the surface flux see it."
    },
    "satratio": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Degree of saturation, smc/smcmax."
    },
    "thks": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/(m*K)",
     "description": "Solid-phase conductivity, 7.7^quartz 2.0^(1-quartz) (quartz against 'other minerals')."
    },
    "xu": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^3/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Unfrozen water volume at saturation, (sh2o/smc) smcmax, the exponent that splits the saturated conductivity between water and ice."
    },
    "thksat": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/(m*K)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Saturated conductivity, thks^(1-smcmax) 2.2^(smcmax-xu) 0.57^xu (ice 2.2, water 0.57 W/(m K))."
    },
    "gammd": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "description": "Dry soil bulk density, (1 - smcmax) 2700."
    },
    "thkdry": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/(m*K)",
     "description": "Dry soil conductivity, (0.135 gammd + 64.7)/(2700 - 0.947 gammd)."
    },
    "ake": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Kersten number, the ice- and water-weighted blend ((smc - sh2o) akei + sh2o akel)/smc, where the frozen part uses akei = satratio and the liquid part the logarithmic akel = log10(satratio) + 1, floored at zero below satratio = 0.1."
    },
    "hcpct": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "J/(m^3*K)",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Volumetric heat capacity of each layer, sh2o ch2o_vol + (1 - smcmax) csoil + (smcmax - smc) cair_vol + (smc - sh2o) cice_vol."
    },
    "t24": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K^4",
     "description": "Fourth power of the air temperature, the linearisation point of the surface emission."
    },
    "yynum": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Net radiation at the linearisation temperature, fdown - emissi sigma t24."
    },
    "yy": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Effective forcing temperature of the linearised surface energy balance, sfctmp + (yynum/rch + th2 - sfctmp - beta epsca)/rr. The skin temperature relaxes towards it."
    },
    "zz1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Coupling strength of the skin temperature to the top soil layer, df1/(0.5 ze[2] rch rr) + 1. zz1 = 1 would mean no conduction and t1 = yy."
    },
    "t1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "DIAGNOSTIC skin temperature, (yy + (zz1 - 1) stc[1])/zz1: a weighted mean of the atmospheric forcing temperature and the top soil layer, not a prognostic state."
    },
    "K_soil": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/(m*K)",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Thermal conductivity at each layer interface: the conductivity of the layer ABOVE the interface, K_soil[kn] = df_layer[kn-1], which is what the Fortran uses and not a centred average (FORTRAN_BUGS N90). The entries at the two domain faces are never read by the lowering, which takes the prescribed F_soil there instead."
    },
    "F_soil": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Prescribed heat flux at each interface, positive DOWNWARD (the +lev direction): the linearised surface energy balance at kn = 1, the conduction towards tbot at kn = NLEV+1, and zero in the interior, where the flux is diffusive."
    },
    "ssoil": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Ground heat flux as WRF reports it, df1 (stc[1] - t1)/(0.5 ze[2]). WRF flips the sign at the end of SFLX so that a positive value WARMS the surface, which makes it the negative of F_soil[1]."
    },
    "t2v": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K",
     "description": "Virtual temperature at the lowest model level, sfctmp (1 + 0.61 q2)."
    },
    "sheat": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "W/m^2",
     "description": "Sensible heat flux, -(ch cp sfcprs/(rd t2v)) (th2 - t1), evaluated at the DIAGNOSTIC skin temperature and with cp = 1004.5, not PENMAN's 1004.6."
    },
    "dstc_dt": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "K/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Instantaneous soil-temperature tendency of each layer, the flux divergence divided by the layer heat capacity. This is the dt -> 0 limit of WRF's (STC_out - STC_in)/dt, whose finite-dt value differs because HSTEP solves the same operator implicitly."
    }
   },
