       "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run at chem_opt = 170 with Noah (sf_surface_physics = 2, num_soil_layers = 4, silt loam, dryland cropland), data/eqwefic/chem170_scm, dumped by ctessum-claude/WRF branch earthsciml-instrumented-chem170 (commit ac6d4cc) and replayed through the real64 (-fdefault-real-8) kernels/noah_driver. Inputs are the dumped SFLX arguments (real32 values widened). df1, yy, zz1 and the pre-step ground heat flux are not Registry variables; they are published by the kernels/noah_esm_*.inc splices into a BUILD-TIME COPY of module_sf_noahlsm.F (the WRF source is untouched). The column is above freezing and snow-free throughout, so the SNKSRC phase-change sink and the SNOPAC branch are inactive here and therefore UNTESTED, not merely unused. SURFACE CLOSURE at second-day noon. SFLX recomputes the surface conductivity df1 from the soil moisture that SMFLX has already advanced, so yy, zz1, t1, ssoil and sheat all carry an O(dt) dependence on the replay step; the reference is therefore taken at ESM_DT = 1e-6 s, where that truncation is below 1e-10 relative. At ESM_DT = 0.01 s the same quantities are already off the dt -> 0 limit by up to 5.7e-7 relative, and WRF's own dt = 60 s values by up to 3e-3.",
